		{
			"id": "note-deletes",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 1410,
			"width": 540,
			"height": 140,
			"text": "## After the loop: deletes\n\nTags and actions removed in the form are deleted once, after all records, with a single `DELETE ... WHERE id IN (...)` per table.",
			"codemap": {
				"kind": "note",
				"title": "After the loop: deletes",
				"category": "note",
				"text": "Tags and actions removed in the form are deleted once, after all records, with a single `DELETE ... WHERE id IN (...)` per table.",
				"textHash": "d321f185"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "note-batching",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 580,
			"y": 1410,
			"width": 540,
			"height": 140,
			"text": "## Result: 2 batches per table\n\nTwo risks give two flushes, so each table receives 2 insert batches instead of one INSERT per row.\n\nRequires `hibernate.jdbc.batch_size=50`, `order_inserts=true`, `order_updates=true`, and SEQUENCE ids (IDENTITY disables batching).",
			"codemap": {
				"kind": "note",
				"title": "Result: 2 batches per table",
				"category": "note",
				"text": "Two risks give two flushes, so each table receives 2 insert batches instead of one INSERT per row.\n\nRequires `hibernate.jdbc.batch_size=50`, `order_inserts=true`, `order_updates=true`, and SEQUENCE ids (IDENTITY disables batching).",
				"textHash": "42fafe7e"
			}
		}
